  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SALAR/Avfall Sverige Waste Management for Ukraine (WM4U)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SKR/Avfall Sverige kommunal avfallshantering Ukraina (WM4U)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let f&#xf6;r programmet &#xe4;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra avfallshanteringen i Ukraina i linje med EU:s direktiv och regler, vilket bidrar till att begr&#xe4;nsa klimatp&#xe5;verkan,&#xa0; &#xf6;kad resurseffektivitet, st&#xe4;rkande av den cirkul&#xe4;ra ekonomin, milj&#xf6;m&#xe4;ssig h&#xe5;llbarhet och f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad livskvalitet f&#xf6;r alla. Insatsen implementeras av Sveriges kommuner och regioner under 2024 - 2027.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal to which the proposed programme will contribute is to improve waste management in Ukraine, with benefits for climate mitigation, resource efficiency, the circular economy, environmental sustainability and quality of life for all. The programme is implemented by the Swedish Association of Local Authorities and Regions (SALAR) during 2024 - 2027.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal to which the proposed programme will contribute is to improve waste management in Ukraine, with benefits for climate mitigation, resource efficiency, the circular economy, environmental sustainability and quality of life for all.

This will be achieved by supporting Ukraine to align to EU rules, laws, standards, directives and regulations and by doing so contribute to Ukraine&apos;s EU accession process regarding Chapter 27 on Environment and Climate. 

The programme is structured around two main areas for support with an expected overall outcome for each:

1. Support for stronger multi-level governance in waste management

Outcome: Improved planning, regulation, financing and coordination between tiers of government with a view to more effective implementation of national legislation and policy on municipal waste management.

2. Support to capacity development in selected municipalities

Outcome: Selected municipalities have strengthened their ability to deliver inclusive and sustainable waste management services.</narrative>
  </description>
